## API for traffic and some crime data and mastodon

1. trafficinjury [GET]  /trafficinjury/{gender}/{year}

    This API returns traffic injury(include different category injury) data filtered by year and gender

    Example calling:

        api_url = "http://localhost:9090/trafficinjury/Male/2021"
        
        response = requests.get(api_url)

        if response.status_code == 200:
            data = response.json().get('Data', [])
            if data:
                print(data)
            else:
                print("No data returned by the API.")
        else:
            print(f"Error: {response.status_code} - {response.text}")

2. trafficagghour [GET] /trafficagghour/{startdate}/{enddate}

    This API returns traffic density aggregate by hour recently in VIC. startdate and enddate is needed.

    Example calling:

        api_url = "http://localhost:9090/trafficaggbyhour/2025-05-05/2025-05-10"

        response = requests.get(api_url)

        if response.status_code == 200:
            data = response.json().get('Data', [])
            if data:
                df = pd.DataFrame(data)
                print(f"Total Records: {len(df)}")
                display(df.head()) 
            else:
                print("No data returned by the API.")
        else:
            print(f"Error: {response.status_code} - {response.text}")

3. trafficvolumeapi [GET] /trafficvolumeapi/{startdate}/{starttime}/{enddate}/{endtime}

    This API returns traffic volume data including coordinates, density, congestion and speed.

    Example calling:

        api_url = "http://localhost:9090/trafficvolume/2025-05-09/12:00:00/2025-05-09/14:00:00"

        response = requests.get(api_url)

        if response.status_code == 200:
            data = response.json().get('Data', [])
            if data:
                df = pd.DataFrame(data)
                print(f"Total Records: {len(df)}")
                display(df.head()) 
            else:
                print("No data returned by the API.")
        else:
            print(f"Error: {response.status_code} - {response.text}")

